<title>USA: Austrian Airlines to buy Pratt engines.</title>
<headline>Austrian Airlines to buy Pratt engines.</headline>
<dateline>EAST HARTFORD, Conn 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pratt &amp; Whitney, a unit of United Technologies Corp, said Monday it had reached an agreement to sell engines to Austrian Airlines for its new aircraft. The deal is worth about $90 million.</p>
<p>Pratt said it agreed to sell the airline four PW4168 engines for its A330 aircraft as part of a joint aircraft/engine evaluation effort with Swissair and Sabena.</p>
<p>Those two airlines bought a combined total of 13 A330s powered by the PW4168 for $290 million two weeks ago.</p>
<p>The company said Austrian Airlines would acquire the engines beginning in 1998.</p>
</text>
